---
id: org.dxos.plugin.assistant
name: AssistantPlugin
version: 0.1.0
---

An AI assistant plugin for DXOS Composer that provides conversational AI, skill-driven automation,
multi-provider LLM support, and deep ECHO integration.

## Extensions

The following extension dialects are used in this document.
Each extension is defined in the Appendix or resolved via its URI.

| Term        | URI                           |
|-------------|-------------------------------|
| `type`      | `org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0`      |
| `feat`      | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0`      |
| `scenario`  | `org.dxos.mdl.scenario@1.0`  |
| `component` | `org.dxos.mdl.component@1.0` |
| `op`        | `org.dxos.mdl.op@1.1`        |
| `test`      | `org.dxos.mdl.test@1.0`      |
| `decision`  | `org.dxos.mdl.decision@1.0`  |

## Types

```mdl
type ModelProvider
  literals: edge | ollama | lmstudio
```

```mdl
type ChatView
  literals: normal | summary | thinking | debug
```

```mdl
type ModelDefaults
  fields:
    edge?: string
    ollama?: string
    lmstudio?: string
```

```mdl
type Settings
  fields:
    customPrompts?: boolean
    chatView?: ChatView
    modelProvider?: ModelProvider
    modelDefaults?: ModelDefaults
    disableCodeMode?: boolean
    reportStruggles?: boolean
    tracePanelDebug?: boolean
```

```mdl
type Chat
  fields:
    id: string
    name?: string
    messages: Message[]
```

```mdl
type Message
  fields:
    id: string
    role: user | assistant | system
    content: string
    timestamp: string
```

```mdl
type SkillForm
  fields:
    key: string
    name: string
    description?: string
```

## Components

```mdl
component ChatPanel
  desc: Main conversational interface for interacting with the AI assistant.
  props:
    chat: Chat
    companionTo?: Obj
  state:
    messages: Message[]
    pending: boolean
    view: ChatView
  slots:
    toolbar?: ReactNode
    empty?: ReactNode
  actions:
    sendMessage(content: string)
    clearHistory()
    switchView(view: ChatView)
  emits:
    onMessage(message: Message)
  layout: |
    ┌─────────────────────────┐
    │ [toolbar slot]          │
    ├─────────────────────────┤
    │                         │
    │  message list           │
    │  [empty slot]           │
    │                         │
    ├─────────────────────────┤
    │  input + send           │
    └─────────────────────────┘
```

```mdl
component TracePanel
  desc: Displays the execution trace of an AI operation as a commit graph or raw JSON.
  props:
    chat: Chat
  state:
    debug: boolean
  actions:
    toggleDebug()
  layout: |
    ┌─────────────────────────┐
    │ trace / span tree       │
    └─────────────────────────┘
```

```mdl
component AssistantSettings
  desc: Settings panel for configuring the AI model provider, model defaults, and chat view.
  props:
    settings: Settings
  emits:
    onChange(settings: Settings)
```

## Operations

```mdl
op CreateChat
  key: org.dxos.operation.assistant.createChat
  desc: Creates a new Chat object and optionally adds it to the active space.
  input:
    db: Database
    name?: string
    addToSpace?: boolean
  output: Chat
  effects: [echo:write]
```

```mdl
op UpdateChatName
  key: org.dxos.operation.assistant.updateChatName
  desc: Automatically derives and updates the name of a chat using the AI service.
  input:
    chat: Chat
  output: void
  effects: [echo:write, ai:infer]
```

```mdl
op AnalyzeTurn
  key: org.dxos.operation.assistant.analyzeTurn
  desc: TurnReviewSkill's background end-request hook. Judges the turn that just ended with a small model and reports it when the agent struggled because of its prompting or tooling.
  input: {}
  output: void
  effects: [echo:read, ai:infer, http:post]
```

```mdl
op SetCurrentChat
  desc: Associates a primary object with a specific companion chat in session state.
  input:
    companionTo: Obj
    chat?: Chat
  output: void
```

```mdl
op RunPromptInNewChat
  desc: Creates a new chat, binds context objects and skills, then runs a prompt.
  note: |
    Operation DEFINED in plugin-routine (RoutineOperation.RunPromptInNewChat)
    so Routine UI and downstream plugins can dispatch it without depending on
    plugin-assistant. The HANDLER (chat creation + AiContext binding) is contributed
    here; see operations/run-prompt-in-new-chat.ts.
```

```mdl
op EnsureCompanionChat
  key: org.dxos.operation.assistant.ensureCompanionChat
  desc: Returns the companion chat for an object, creating one if none exists.
  input:
    db: Database
    companionTo: Obj
  output:
    chat: Chat
    persisted: boolean
  effects: [echo:write]
```

```mdl
op OnCreateSpace
  desc: Provisions initial assistant objects when a new space is created.
  input:
    space: Space
    rootCollection: Collection
  output: void
  effects: [echo:write]
```

```mdl
op ToggleTracePanelDebug
  key: org.dxos.operation.assistant.setTracePanelDebug
  desc: Toggles the trace panel between commit-graph and raw JSON debug view.
  input:
    state?: boolean
  output: boolean
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: AI Chat

  req F-1.1: User can create a new Chat object in any space.
  req F-1.2: User can type a message and receive a streamed AI response.
  req F-1.3: Chat history is persisted to ECHO and replicated to all peers.
  req F-1.4:
    when: chat has enough messages
    then: chat name is automatically derived from the conversation
```

```mdl
feat F-2: Companion Chat

  req F-2.1:
    when: user opens an object that supports companions
    then: a companion chat panel is shown alongside the object
  req F-2.2:
    when: companion chat does not yet exist
    then: op:EnsureCompanionChat creates one and optionally persists it
  req F-2.3:
    when: op:EnsureCompanionChat resolves a companion chat
    then: op:BindChatContext runs every cap:SubjectContext contribution that applies to the primary
      object and binds the merged result — by default the object itself plus the skills its type
      declares via Skill.SkillsAnnotation
```

```mdl
feat F-3: Skill System

  req F-3.1: Skills define named AI configurations (instructions, tools, model).
  req F-3.2: Built-in skills include: Assistant, Browser, Database, WebSearch, Discord, Linear, Agent, Planning, Memory, Automation, SkillManager.
  req F-3.3:
    when: user selects a skill for a chat
    then: chat uses that skill's instructions and tool set
  req F-3.4: op:RunPromptInNewChat accepts skill keys to bind before sending the prompt.
```

```mdl
feat F-4: Multi-Provider LLM

  req F-4.1: Supported providers: DXOS Edge (remote), Ollama (local), LM Studio (local).
  req F-4.2: User can configure the active provider and per-provider default model in Settings.
  req F-4.3:
    when: the active provider is unavailable
    then: AiService falls back to the next registered resolver
```

```mdl
feat F-5: Tool Execution

  req F-5.1: The assistant skill exposes LayoutOperation.Open and NavigationOperation.ResolveNavigationTargets
             as tools. Both are owned elsewhere — the assistant contributes no navigation operation of its
             own, so an agent resolving an object to a path uses the same entry point the UI does.
  req F-5.2: Web search tool is registered via WebSearchToolkit.
  req F-5.3:
    when: AI invokes a tool during a conversation
    then: operation is dispatched via the compute runtime and result returned to the model
  req F-5.4: Code mode is on by default and opt-out via `Settings.disableCodeMode`; the host supplies the engine
             through the `codeModeTurnProducer` plugin option, and without it the setting has no effect.
  req F-5.5:
    when: Settings.disableCodeMode is not set, the host supplied a code-mode producer, and no AgentTurnProducer is contributed
    then: agent processes spawned afterwards run turns through the code-mode producer (one `eval` tool)
          instead of AiSession
```

```mdl
feat F-6: ECHO Integration

  req F-6.1: Chat, Skill, Feed, Message, Memory, Plan, Routine, Agent, McpServer, and Sequence schemas are registered with ECHO. A chat's subject is recorded by Chat.CompanionChatAnnotation on that subject, not by a type.
  req F-6.2:
    when: a new space is created
    then: op:OnCreateSpace provisions default assistant objects
  req F-6.3: AiContext.Binding schema supports binding ECHO objects as named context variables in a conversation.
```

```mdl
feat F-7: Execution Trace

  req F-7.1: Every AI operation produces a structured span tree captured in the TracePanel.
  req F-7.2: User can toggle between commit-graph and raw JSON views via op:ToggleTracePanelDebug.
```

```mdl
feat F-8: Agent Struggle Reports

  req F-8.1: Reporting is opt-in via `Settings.reportStruggles`, off by default, and also requires telemetry to be enabled.
  req F-8.2:
    when: the chat processor issues a request with reporting enabled
    then: TurnReviewSkill is bound to the chat; its end-request hook (op:AnalyzeTurn) runs in the background, so
          the request settles without waiting for the review and the agent process awaits it before finishing
  req F-8.3:
    when: the reviewer judges the agent struggled from missing/wrong instructions or a missing/faulty tool
    then: the trajectory is uploaded to the feedback-logs bucket under `trajectories/` and an `agent_struggle` event is captured
          carrying the cause, model DXN, code mode, and enabled skills
  req F-8.4: A review that fails is logged and dropped; it never surfaces to the user.
```

## Acceptance

```mdl
scenario T-1: Create chat and send message
  given: a space is open and the assistant plugin is active
  when: user creates a new Chat and sends "Hello"
  then:
    - Chat object appears in the space
    - AI response is appended to Chat.messages
    - Chat is persisted to ECHO
```

```mdl
scenario T-2: Companion chat provisioning
  given: user opens a document with no companion chat
  when: companion panel initializes
  then:
    - op:EnsureCompanionChat creates a new Chat
    - persisted === false until user sends a message
```

```mdl
scenario T-3: Skill binding
  given: a chat exists
  when: user binds the "WebSearch" skill key
  then:
    - skill instructions are applied to the next AI request
    - web search tool is available in the tool list
```

```mdl
scenario T-4: Model provider switch
  given: assistant settings are open
  when: user switches provider from edge to ollama
  then:
    - Settings.modelProvider === ollama
    - next AI request is routed to the Ollama resolver
```

```mdl
scenario T-5: Run prompt in background
  given: a database and a prompt string are available
  when: op:RunPromptInNewChat is called with background: true
  then:
    - a new Chat is created and returned
    - the prompt runs via compute runtime without opening the UI
```

```mdl
scenario T-7: Trace panel debug toggle
  given: trace panel is showing commit-graph view
  when: op:ToggleTracePanelDebug is invoked with no argument
  then:
    - tracePanelDebug setting flips to true
    - trace panel switches to raw JSON view
```

## QA

Executable tests. Each step carries a human instruction (`do`) and, where the step maps to an
invocable operation, an agent binding (`invoke`). Report failures by test and step number.

```mdl
test QA-1: Create a chat and send a message
  desc: The core assistant round-trip — create a Chat, send a prompt, get a streamed AI response.
  actors: both
  covers: [F-1.1, F-1.2, F-1.3, F-1.4, T-1]
  status: unverified
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open
    - no Chat named "QA Chat" exists — ABORT rather than deleting one this test did not create
  steps:
    - name: Create the chat
      do: Open the assistant panel and click "New chat".
      invoke: [op:CreateChat] { name: "QA Chat" }
      capture: created
      expect: a new Chat named "QA Chat" opens, empty
      assert: return !!$created.object
      note: |
        CreateChat returns the chat UNFILED — the handler adds its feed regardless, but persisting
        it in the space is a separate step (see plugin-space's addObject), which the UI's "New
        chat" gesture does implicitly.
    - name: Send a message
      do: Type "Hello" into the chat input and press Enter.
      expect: "Hello" appears as a user message, followed by a streamed assistant response, and
        the chat is persisted to ECHO and replicated to peers
      note: |
        NO `invoke` — sending a prompt runs through the AI streaming path (`AiSession`), not
        through the operation invoker; there is no `SendMessage` operation to call directly.
    - name: Chat is auto-named
      do: (no gesture — happens automatically once the chat has enough messages)
      invoke: [op:UpdateChatName] { chat: $created.object }
      expect: the chat's name changes from "QA Chat" to something derived from the conversation
      assert: return typeof $result === 'undefined' || true;
      note: |
        `UpdateChatName` returns void — verify the effect on `chat.name`, not the return value
        (Execution Rule 3). Included here for completeness; a fast QA pass may treat this as
        `given` already established rather than re-triggering it.
  after:
    - name: Delete the chat
      do: Right-click "QA Chat" in the navtree and choose Delete.
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.removeObjects { objects: [$created.object], target: $given.space.db }
      expect: the row leaves the navtree and its plank closes if it was open
```

```mdl
test QA-2: Companion chat is provisioned and bound
  desc: op:EnsureCompanionChat + op:BindChatContext — the chat a companioned object gets automatically.
  actors: both
  covers: [F-2.1, F-2.2, F-2.3, T-2]
  status: unverified
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open
    - subject: a Document in the space that has no companion chat yet
  steps:
    - name: Ensure the companion chat
      do: Open the document; the companion chat panel initializes automatically.
      invoke: [op:EnsureCompanionChat] { companionTo: $given.subject }
      capture: ensured
      expect: a new Chat is returned and NOT yet persisted (`persisted === false`)
      assert: return $result.persisted === false && !!$result.chat;
    - name: Bind chat context
      do: (no separate gesture — panel initialization runs this immediately after ensuring the chat)
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.assistant.bindChatContext { chat: $ensured.chat, subject: $given.subject }
      note: No `op BindChatContext` block is declared above — referenced by its full runtime key.
      expect: the companion chat's context now includes the document (and any skills its type
        declares via Skill.SkillsAnnotation)
  after:
    - name: (nothing to undo)
      do: The companion chat is never persisted unless a message is sent, so nothing was written
        to the space.
      expect: the document still has no persisted companion chat
```

```mdl
test QA-3: The prompt carries context, commands and the agent's settings
  desc: |
    The chat prompt: the task and context drawers above it, the "+" menu (objects and MCP servers),
    `@` mentions, `/` commands and skills, and the agent picker (agent, where it runs, model).
  actors: human
  status: unverified
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open
    - documents "Prompt redesign spec", "Q4 roadmap" and "Meeting notes", a person "Rich Burdon",
      and MCP servers "Linear" and "GitHub", both switched off
    - chat: a chat "Prompt redesign" with two tasks, open in a plank
  steps:
    - name: Open the task and context drawers
      do: Click the tasks button in the group before the microphone and Send, then the context button.
      expect: the two tasks open in a drawer above the prompt; the context button swaps it for a drawer
        with Context and a collapsed Skills section, and only one drawer is open at a time
    - name: Switch on an MCP server from the + menu
      do: Click "+", open "MCP servers", check "Linear", then uncheck it.
      expect: Linear shows a check and the menu stays open for the next switch; MCP servers are not
        listed in the context drawer, since the switch is the space's rather than the chat's
    - name: Load a skill with a slash command
      do: Type "/web", pick "/web-search", then press Enter.
      expect: the thread shows "Loaded the Web Search skill." and Web Search appears under Skills
    - name: Create a task with a slash command
      do: Type "/task:create Draft the launch note" and press Enter.
      expect: with the tasks drawer open, the task appears in it
    - name: Change the model and where the agent runs
      do: Open the agent picker; pick another model, then switch "Agent runs on" to EDGE and back.
      expect: the trigger names the new model, and its icon is a cloud while the agent runs on EDGE
    - name: Compose a message with mentions
      do: Add "Rich Burdon" with "+" > "Add an object…", then mention "Prompt redesign spec" and
        "Q4 roadmap" with "@".
      expect: each object shows in the prompt as a chip; Context does not change while composing
    - name: Attach a file
      do: Add a file with "+" > "Add files…".
      expect: the file is listed as attaching until it is stored, then shows as a chip where it was added
    - name: Send the message
      do: Press Enter.
      expect: the three objects join Context, the sent question shows their names, and a reply
        streams in
    - name: Switch the thread view
      do: Pick "Summary" from the toolbar's View menu, then type "/view normal".
      expect: the thread switches to the summary view and back
    - name: Remove an object from context
      do: Click the x beside Rich Burdon in the context drawer.
      expect: Rich Burdon leaves Context; the message that mentioned them is unchanged
```

## Changelog

```mdl
decision D-1: The chat prompt follows Claude Code: one picker chooses the agent, where it runs and its model; skills load as `/` commands; `@` inserts a mention of an object, which joins the chat's context when the message is sent; a "+" menu adds files, objects, commands and MCP servers.
  date: 2026-10-21
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [QA-3]
```

```mdl
decision D-2: The chat's tasks and its context are two drawers above the prompt, opened from a group of buttons before the microphone and Send, one open at a time; other plugins add their own sections to the context drawer.
  date: 2026-10-21
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [QA-3]
```

```mdl
decision D-3: The `@` menu runs a full-text search as the reader types, debounced, and is the same search the markdown editor's `@` menu uses.
  date: 2026-10-21
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [QA-3]
```

```mdl
decision D-4: Enter in the `@` menu picks the row on screen and drops the search still running.
  date: 2026-10-21
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [QA-3]
```

```mdl
decision D-5: MCP servers are switched on and off in the "+" menu and are not listed in the context drawer. Fills in [D-1] and [D-2].
  date: 2026-10-21
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [QA-3]
  why: The switch is the space's, not the chat's; listed in a chat's context it would read as something that chat holds.
  rejected:
    - List enabled servers in the context drawer: switching one off there would change every chat in the space.
```

```mdl
decision D-6: An attached file is stored in the space and mentioned where it was added; the prompt lists files still attaching and those that could not be stored, with why, and does not send while any is attaching. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-21
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [QA-3]
  why: A message sent before its file is stored would name a file the agent cannot read, and a failure shown only in the thread is missed on the space-home prompt, which has none.
  rejected:
    - Report failures as the chat's error event: the space-home prompt renders no thread to show it.
```

```mdl
decision D-7: The attaching list appears only once an upload has taken 400 ms, in a neutral banner, so a quick upload does not flash. Fills in [D-6].
  date: 2026-10-21
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [QA-3]
  why: A local upload stores in a fraction of a second, which showed the banner for one frame.
```

```mdl
decision D-8: Approve [D-7].
  date: 2026-10-21
  by: user:wittjosiah
```

```mdl
decision D-9: Code mode is the default turn engine; the setting becomes `disableCodeMode`, an opt-out.
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-5.4, F-5.5]
```

